Z||000000||rodmcneill||06-17-2001||08:10 PM||||Besides Held is anyone making drop spindles for the front of a 88?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Toddster||06-17-2001||09:01 PM||||No. It's that simple. BUT, I have a set of Held Spindles (when Ryane was still making them). I thought about making a few copies for future projects. It does not look too complex, The steel is simple mild steel and I have the welding equipment for it. All I would need to do is make a set of jigs.<P>I'd be happy to send you the dimensions so you could make your own.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||06-17-2001||09:40 PM||||Toddster, could you send them to me (dimensions)?  I would appreciate it.  Front and rear coil overs would be sweet.<P>thanks<BR>fiero5sp@home.com||||reg||6
Z||000003||skitime||06-17-2001||09:52 PM||||Are the Held spindles still available and if so how much are they? Toddster would you sell your or are you going to use them?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||06-18-2001||01:20 AM||||Snorts and spits a loogy...<P>makeup '88 drop spindles... yep, weekend project.<P>email sent.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 06-18-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000005||Toddster||06-18-2001||01:18 PM||||I'm going to use these on a new project I'm starting as soon as the Ferrari 355 project is finished this summer. So, sorry folks, not for sale.<P>But making them is not hard. I have my own Mig Welder and I'm pretty good with it. All I need to do is take the measurements, call my local steel supplier and have them cut to measure, stick it all in a jig and weld it up. <P>Ryane Powdercoated them which is probably a good idea so I would have to Farm that job out but I have heard that Eastwood has a home Powdercoating kit. Don't know what the Mrs. would think of me baking car parts in the oven though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Give me a few days to get the measurements and I'll post them here.||||reg||14
Z||000006||rodmcneill||06-18-2001||06:18 PM||||Thanks for the replies guys. I called Street Dreams like you suggested Tigger, they make drop spindles for 84-87 Fiero's. I talked to the owner and I guess the idea of 88 drop spindles is way way way on the back burner. Too bad. Now Toddster when you give the measurements for your spindles please give the drop measurement. I see the Held units come in 1", 1 1/2" and 2" drop. If you go more than 1" you can not use the stock 15" wheels according to their web page info. If you decide to produce these let me know, price etc.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Toddster||06-18-2001||07:54 PM||||The one's I have are 1 1/2 drop. But that is why I want to make a jig. then all I ned to do is raise or lower the jig before welding to vary the drop.<P>Measurements up soon!||||reg||1
Z||000008||G-Nasty||06-18-2001||10:56 PM||||I believe my Bel-Tec spindles are forged-made into their shape. I was hit in the front by a 17 yr old chick in a lincoln. The crash bent my upper control arm and then kinked my koni shock. Did not phase my spindle forged in hell. I dont think tack-welding the spindle around the sides would give you enough strength. That same spindle is on my new 87GT --<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Toddster||06-19-2001||01:52 PM||||G-Nasty, I agree. "Tack welding" would not work, but seem welding is stronger than the original steel.<P>I am going to put up some pictures on my web site in a couple days and then I will list the measurments and drawings tomorrow. They are almost done.<P>Please be good to me people. I am not a professional draftsman. But I'll try to make them as clear as possible.<P>There are 8 critcal measurements and the best way to make sure they are accurate is to compare them to a factory spindle. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||artherd||06-20-2001||05:55 AM||||I have to suggest guys, just buy the Held/Ryane parts.<P>Expensive? Not really compared to what else is out there for other cars.<P>Plus, your LIFE depends on these parts, no two ways about it.<P>My feelings anyway.<BR>(I'm ordering the Ryane/Held setup for all 4 corners of my car)<P>Best!<BR>Ben<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000011||Toddster||06-20-2001||07:18 PM||||Here are the measurements:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.concentric.net/~Atamelio/Pontiac.shtml" TARGET=_blank>http://www.concentric.net/~Atamelio/Pontiac.shtml</A> <P>A couple of points: there is one part missing. The reason is because it will vary in size depending on the amount of drop. You will see it in the pics I post tomorrow. Use your judgements on measurements.<P>REMEMBER that each spindle is a mirror of the other. These drawings relate to the driver side unit. <P>Most machine shops will have no trouble making these items up but from the units that I have it appears that parts 5, 6 and the brake caliper bolt holes seem to be "cut" from a real '88 spindle and welded in place here. Although not stated in the measurements the caliper bolt holes are slightly thicker than the rest of the steel, hence my conclusion about being welded in.<P>Feel free to send questions.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
